<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Menem decrees union health-care reform.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Menem decrees union health-care reform.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Carlos Menem signed a controversial decree deregulating the country's union-controlled health-care system and allowing Argentines to choose their own medical plans, the government said Monday.</p>
<p>Argentina now has about 300 union-controlled health plans financed by mandatory contributions, which bring in about $2.5 billion a year to the unions.</p>
</text>
